A script procedure named Constructor (diag.constructor_outside_class,
warning): outside a class it is just an oddly named procedure. A procedure
with another name in the same script is the near miss.
-- input.ssl --
:PROCEDURE Constructor;
	:PARAMETERS sName;
	:DECLARE sLabel;
	sLabel := "Built " + sName;
	:RETURN sLabel;
:ENDPROC;

:PROCEDURE Build;
	:PARAMETERS sName;
	:RETURN DoProc("Constructor", {sName});
:ENDPROC;
-- format --
:PROCEDURE Constructor;
	:PARAMETERS sName;
	:DECLARE sLabel;

	sLabel := "Built " + sName;

	:RETURN sLabel;
:ENDPROC;

:PROCEDURE Build;
	:PARAMETERS sName;

	:RETURN DoProc("Constructor", {sName});
:ENDPROC;
-- diagnostics --
1:1-1:12 warning constructor_outside_class: 'Constructor' is only meaningful inside a ':CLASS' definition
-- diagnostics [--strict --info] --
1:1-1:12 warning constructor_outside_class: 'Constructor' is only meaningful inside a ':CLASS' definition
